  "lineage": "Mid-2000s Atlanta hip-hop subgenre developed from crunk through stripped-back minimal production replacing crunk's aggressive synth-and-808 with finger-snap-percussion-led beats. D4L's \"Laffy Taffy\" (2005) and Dem Franchize Boyz' \"Lean Wit It, Rock Wit It\" (2005) inaugurated the genre; Yung Joc, Soulja Boy (whose 2007 \"Crank That\" extended snap into broader commercial mainstream), and the Mojoe-and-Drumma-Boy production lineage constitute the canonical roster.",
